[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:A Thirsty Ghost]
[00:14.40]What evidence is there of a ghost?
[00:20.44]A public house which was recently bought by Mr.Ian Thompson is up for sale.
[00:28.18]Mr.Thompson is going to sell it because it is haunted.
[00:33.96]He told me that he could not go to sleep one night
[00:37.94]because he heard a strange noise coming from the bar.
[00:43.12]The next morning,
[00:44.99]he found that the doors had been blocked by chairs and the furniture had been moved.
[00:52.40]Though Mr.Thompson had turned the lights off before he went to bed,
[00:57.50]they were on in the morning.
[01:00.53]He also said that he had found five empty whisky bottles
[01:05.48]which the ghost must have drunk the night before.
[01:09.86]When I suggested that some villagers must have come in for a free drink, Mr.Thompson shook his head.
[01:19.09]The villagers have told him that they will not accept the pub even if he gives it away.
